& [CorrectiveLineage] is mandatory
  + base source used generic Directory where the closed prerequisite enum requires RootDirectory
  + correction snapshot 1616efd9-aad3-437a-9635-1ac9cc00ab6f supersedes that meaning only for root observation kind
  + original source and pre-correction SJS hashes remain immutable history and are not current authority
  + canonical root structural scope is absent relative_path plus TopologyEntryKind::RootDirectory exactly
  + Directory remains the distinct nonroot directory variant
  - never: normalize, alias, coerce, or compare Directory as RootDirectory

& [TermRoles] are closed
  + [left] is first positional supplied operand only
  + [right] is second positional supplied operand only
  + [current_rederived] means exact replay through the present pure prerequisite function, never physical freshness
  + [comparable] means exact profiles, complete limits, and root identity scope agree
  + [Equal] means comparable canonical sequence digest values are byte equal under the exact encoding profile and ordinary SHA-256 collision assumptions
  + [Different] means comparable canonical sequence digest values are byte unequal
  + [scope_fault] means no honest pair disposition exists because operands name different profiles, ceilings, or roots
  - never: use before, after, stable, unchanged, repeated, double_inventory, quiescent_double_inventory, snapshot, receipt, or admitted as result meaning

& [PlanContract] is strict and bounded
  + [type] WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigestReconciliationPlan
  + [profile] is exact cantor-windows-supplied-ordered-topology-inventory-digest-reconciliation/0.1
  + [reconciliation_identity] is a nonzero u64 caller correlation value
  + [encoded_maximum] is 4096 bytes before JSON decode
  + derive Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, and Deserialize with deny_unknown_fields
  + immutable getters expose profile and reconciliation_identity
  + malformed, overlong, unknown, missing, wrong-profile, and zero-identity values reject
  - never: add operand, digest, root, limits, expected disposition, time, deadline, policy, receipt, or admission fields

& [InputContract] is exactly two complete output-only carriers
  + [type] WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigest
  + public transform consumes plan, left, and right by value
  + left and right each retain exact digest plan, complete assembly, profiles, and ordered_inventory_sha256
  + no public overload accepts references as success ownership, digest strings, byte arrays, plans, assemblies, members, observations, roots, vectors, or caller disposition
  + input and output private construction remains prerequisite and current-module authority only

& [PublicFunctions] are exact
  + decode_windows_supplied_ordered_topology_inventory_digest_reconciliation_plan accepts &[u8] and returns strict plan or reconciliation fault
  + decode_and_reconcile_windows_supplied_ordered_topology_inventory_digests accepts plan bytes plus left and right complete carriers by value
  + reconcile_windows_supplied_ordered_topology_inventory_digests accepts decoded plan plus left and right complete carriers by value
  + no other public constructor, transform, raw-input, bare-digest, mutable, physical, temporal, or receipt function exists

& [ValidationPrecedence] is deterministic
  + encoded plan byte bound
  + strict JSON decode
  + exact reconciliation profile
  + nonzero reconciliation identity
  + complete left current rederivation
  + complete right current rederivation
  + exact left and right result profile
  + exact left and right encoding profile
  + exact retained left and right digest-plan result and encoding profiles
  + exact left and right assembly profile
  + complete TopologyScanLimits equality
  + left and right root-first structural extraction
  + absent root relative path on both sides
  + RootDirectory kind on both sides
  + root volume serial equality
  + root lowercase file identity equality
  + digest byte comparison and disposition selection
  + complete result construction
  - never: continue after the first failure

& [CurrentRederivation] is exact on each side
  + clone left.plan and left.assembly through immutable getters
  + call derive_windows_supplied_ordered_topology_inventory_digest with those clones
  + require the complete rederived value to equal complete supplied left
  + on prerequisite error return LeftDigest with side Left and exact nested fault
  + on complete inequality return Internal or LeftDigest contradiction according to the closed implementation mapping before any right work
  + repeat independently for right after left success
  + right failure uses RightDigest and side Right
  + prerequisite canonical writer, tag grammar, hashing, and validation are reused only by function call
  - never: duplicate encoder code, hash again, compare the bare supplied digest before rederivation, or discard nested provenance

& [ProfileScope] is exact
  + both carrier profiles equal cantor-windows-supplied-ordered-topology-inventory-digest/0.1
  + both carrier encoding profiles equal cantor-ordered-topology-observation-encoding/0.1
  + both retained digest plans repeat those two exact values
  + both retained assembly profiles equal cantor-windows-supplied-topology-inventory-assembly/0.1
  + any mismatch returns ScopeProfile before limits or root comparison
  + no version alias, default, compatibility shim, or migration exists

& [LimitScope] is complete exact equality
  + compare the entire left.assembly.plan.limits value with the entire right value
  + equality includes maximum_entries, maximum_depth, maximum_path_bytes, maximum_file_bytes, maximum_total_bytes, maximum_streams_per_entry, and deadline_tick
  + unequal values return Limits before root or digest comparison
  + equal limits establish common declared capability ceilings only
  - never: infer observed completeness, choose one side, merge values, ignore deadline_tick, or hash limits into the prerequisite digest

& [RootScope] is exact structural and strong identity
  + each prerequisite assembly already validates one root-first member
  + implementation nevertheless obtains first member through safe checked access and faults if absent
  + each root observation relative_path is None
  + each root observation kind is TopologyEntryKind::RootDirectory
  + common root volume serial is exact u64 equality
  + common root file ID is exact validated lowercase 32-hex string equality
  + mismatch of path, kind, volume, or file ID returns RootScope
  + mode class, attributes, number_of_links, streams, length, content_sha256, and observation_ordinal remain canonical sequence content and never scope
  + projection, entry-reference, preflight, stability, plan, and carrier identities remain lineage and never root scope

& [CommonScopeRecord] is private and inspectable
  + [type] WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigestReconciliationScope
  + derive Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, and Serialize only
  + private fields are encoding_profile, limits, root_relative_path, root_kind, root_volume_serial, and root_file_id
  + immutable getters expose complete values
  + construction occurs only after exact equality gates
  + record duplicates no digest and creates no authority beyond comparable supplied scope

& [DispositionContract] is closed
  + [type] WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigestReconciliationDisposition
  + variants are Equal and Different
  + Serialize uses snake-case equal and different
  + Equal is selected only when validated ordered_inventory_sha256 strings are exact byte equal
  + Different is selected only when those strings are byte unequal
  + Different is ordinary successful evidence and never a fault
  + no bool, optional, expected value, changed field, first ordinal, cause, direction, or time exists

& [OutputContract] is complete and nonforgeable
  + [type] WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigestReconciliation
  + derive Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, and Serialize only
  + private fields are profile, plan, left, right, common_scope, and disposition
  + immutable getters expose all six fields
  + success owns each original input exactly once and preserves argument order
  + no Deserialize, Default, From, Into, public fields, public constructor, mutable getter, or partial result exists
  + swapping operands never creates time meaning and may change serialized lineage while preserving disposition

& [FaultContract] is closed, bounded, and atomic
  + [code_type] WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigestReconciliationFaultCode
  + [codes] are Json, Profile, ReconciliationIdentity, LeftDigest, RightDigest, ScopeProfile, Limits, RootScope, Resource, and Internal
  + [side_type] WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigestReconciliationSide with Left and Right
  + [fault_type] WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigestReconciliationFault
  + public fault fields are code, side, nested_digest_fault, field, and message
  + LeftDigest requires side Left and one nested digest fault when prerequisite transform fails
  + RightDigest requires side Right and one nested digest fault when prerequisite transform fails
  + all other codes have no side and no nested fault
  + internal complete-rederivation contradiction may omit nested fault but must retain exact side and bounded generic message
  + field is at most 64 Unicode scalars and message at most 256 Unicode scalars
  + Display and Error are implemented without leaking operand or digest content
  + no fault contains a plan, digest string, carrier, assembly, observation, common scope, disposition, or partial result

& [CorrelationAndOrder] remain lineage only
  + reconciliation_identity, commitment_identity, assembly_identity, projection_identity, and entry_reference_identity are never compared across operands for scope or disposition
  + all remain inspectable in retained plan or carriers
  + left-right argument order is retained exactly and never sorted
  + ordered-member order remains inside each canonical digest subject
  - never: infer baseline, candidate, earlier, later, trusted, preferred, or authoritative side

& [EvidenceGrade] is comparable supplied canonical sequence pair only
  + each operand inherits supplied, carrier-projected, structurally assembled, current-revalidated, and canonically committed grades
  + each operand gains current_rederived at this boundary
  + pair gains scope_correlated
  + result gains pair_equal or pair_different
  + physical_origin, physically_observed, acquisition_ordered, enumerated_complete, temporally_stable, double_inventory, quiescent_double_inventory, receipted, admitted, mutated, sealed, and promoted are absent

& [EffectContract] is zero
  + deterministic in-memory byte bound, JSON decode, cloning, prerequisite pure transform calls, exact comparison, bounded diagnostics, and owned result construction only
  + no unsafe, windows-sys, Windows API, filesystem, path resolution, handle, pointer, process, environment, clock, randomness, network, persistence, database, model, Git, tool, fixture, traversal, physical inventory, mutation, seal, test-execution effect, cleanup, or promotion
  + no Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, dependency, feature, unsafe-count, platform-call, or effect delta

& [RequirementSet] is atomic
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-001] strict 4096-byte plan with exact reconciliation profile and nonzero identity
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-002] exactly two complete output-only digest-carrier inputs by value and no lower overload
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-003] independent current complete rederivation of left then right through the proven digest transform
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-004] exact digest, encoding, retained-plan, and assembly profile gates
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-005] exact complete TopologyScanLimits comparison
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-006] exact absent root path, RootDirectory kind, root volume serial, and file identity scope
